\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Topic 1- Elderly Mobility.
\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f0\b\fs32 Prompt 1- Generate 10 innovative ideas for improving elderly mobility in urban environments. Focus on practical and impactful solutions.
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf0 Answer-\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Adaptive Smart Crosswalks\uc0\u8232 Install crosswalks with motion sensors that detect slower walkers and automatically extend crossing time. Add brighter lighting, audio cues, and non-slip surfaces for safer navigation.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Neighborhood Mobility Pods\uc0\u8232 Deploy small, electric, on-demand shuttle pods designed specifically for seniors, with low floors, handrails, and simple voice-activated booking systems for short local trips.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Rest-and-Go Walking Corridors\uc0\u8232 Create designated pedestrian routes with frequent shaded benches, water stations, public toilets, and emergency call buttons so older adults can walk longer distances comfortably.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Senior-Friendly Navigation App + Physical Kiosks\uc0\u8232 Develop a simple app and matching street kiosks that show the safest walking routes, nearest elevators, ramps, benches, pharmacies, and accessible transit stops.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Universal Sidewalk Upgrade Program\uc0\u8232 Redesign sidewalks with smoother pavement, curb ramps, anti-slip materials, wider paths for walkers/wheelchairs, and better maintenance to eliminate trip hazards.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Priority Public Transport Access Zones\uc0\u8232 Reserve easy-access boarding areas near bus/train doors for elderly passengers, with raised platforms, seating while waiting, and staff or volunteers during peak hours.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Wearable Mobility Assistance Network\uc0\u8232 Provide optional smart wearables that detect falls, offer GPS guidance, and connect instantly to caregivers or city emergency services if assistance is needed outdoors.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Intergenerational Walking Companion Program\uc0\u8232 Match students or volunteers with elderly residents for scheduled walks, errands, or transit trips, improving both mobility confidence and social connection.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Micro-Mobility Devices for Seniors\uc0\u8232 Introduce stable, seated e-scooters or lightweight electric walkers with safety features like speed limits, obstacle detection, and dedicated parking/charging stations.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Age-Friendly Urban Planning Score System\uc0\u8232 Create a public city rating system that scores neighborhoods based on senior mobility factors\'97walkability, transport access, safety, and accessibility\'97to drive policy improvements and investment.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Prompt 2- Generate 10 ideas for improving elderly mobility in cities that are completely unlike existing solutions.\'a0
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Constraints:
\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f0\b\fs32 - Do not use apps, AI, smartphones, or digital platforms
\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f0\b\fs32 - Avoid common ideas like ride-sharing, wearables, or tracking systems
\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f0\b\fs32 - Focus on unconventional, non-obvious approaches
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf0 Answer-\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Moving Handrail Streets\uc0\u8232 Install slow-moving continuous handrails along key walking routes\'97similar to airport moving walkways but designed as supportive rails rather than full conveyors\'97helping seniors maintain balance and reduce walking effort.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Seasonal Mobility Streets\uc0\u8232 Create \'93winter-safe\'94 and \'93summer-safe\'94 priority routes where city crews actively adjust surfaces by season: heated pavement in winter, mist-cooled shaded walkways in summer, and wind-protected corridors year-round.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Public Errand Exchange Boards\uc0\u8232 Set up physical community boards in neighborhoods where residents can post small errands (carrying groceries, accompanying someone to the doctor), creating spontaneous local support without formal services.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sit-First Bus Stops\uc0\u8232 Redesign bus stops so seating is the main feature rather than an afterthought: enclosed chair circles, leaning supports, armrest-assisted standing, and queue systems built around seated waiting.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Slow-Lane Streets\uc0\u8232 Designate entire neighborhood streets as \'93slow mobility lanes\'94 where bicycles, carts, mobility aids, and pedestrians share protected ultra-low-speed space without pressure from fast walkers or traffic.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Urban Walking Hosts\uc0\u8232 Employ trained street-based assistants stationed in busy districts whose sole role is helping older adults cross roads, carry bags, navigate stairs, or provide physical walking support when needed.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Destination Clustering Policy\uc0\u8232 Require essential services\'97pharmacies, clinics, groceries, post offices\'97to be physically clustered within short walking distances so seniors need fewer separate trips across the city.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Bench Libraries\uc0\u8232 Instead of random seating, create mapped \'93bench libraries\'94 where benches are designed for different needs: recovery benches, social benches, leaning benches, stretch benches, and weather-protected rest spots.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Public Push-Cart Network\uc0\u8232 Provide lightweight shared neighborhood push-carts for groceries, laundry, or personal transport\'97stored at common points like shopping carts, but optimized for walking support and daily errands.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Quiet Crossing Hours\uc0\u8232 Introduce daily scheduled low-noise, low-traffic periods in dense neighborhoods where delivery vehicles, loud construction, and heavy traffic pause, making streets calmer and less stressful for elderly movement.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Prompt 3- Generate 10 ideas for improving elderly mobility in cities inspired by systems from nature, biology, or non-urban environments.
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Focus on translating principles (e.g. swarm behavior, ecosystems, circulation systems) into urban mobility solutions.
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf0 Answer-\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Capillary Path Networks (Inspired by Blood Circulation)\uc0\u8232 Design cities with dense \'93capillary\'94 walking paths branching from major streets directly into residential zones, so seniors can reach daily needs through short, low-stress routes instead of relying on large arterial roads.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Migration Corridor Mobility Routes (Inspired by Animal Migration)\uc0\u8232 Create protected seasonal walking corridors linking homes to markets, clinics, and parks\'97clear, obstacle-free routes that guide predictable daily movement like migration paths in nature.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Mycelium Support Hubs (Inspired by Fungal Networks)\uc0\u8232 Build small interconnected neighborhood support points\'97benches, water, toilets, helpers, repair stations\'97spread like mycelium nodes, so mobility support exists everywhere rather than only at central locations.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Bird Perch Resting System (Inspired by Perching Behavior)\uc0\u8232 Place frequent elevated leaning posts, short-rest stools, and hand supports along sidewalks, allowing quick \'93pause points\'94 instead of requiring full benches, similar to how birds conserve energy through brief perches.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Shade Canopy Ecosystems (Inspired by Forest Layers)\uc0\u8232 Develop layered walking streets with trees, vines, awnings, and pergolas creating natural climate-controlled corridors where older adults can move comfortably without exposure to harsh sun, wind, or rain.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Tide-Based Street Scheduling (Inspired by Ocean Tides)\uc0\u8232 Organize urban activity in rhythmic waves: certain streets become quieter and pedestrian-priority during predictable times each day, allowing seniors to move during safe \'93low tide\'94 traffic periods.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ant Trail Navigation Design (Inspired by Ant Colony Paths)\uc0\u8232 Use highly visible, intuitive ground markings and physical cues\'97textures, colors, landmarks\'97to create naturally followable routes to key destinations without relying on signs or maps.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Root Zone Stability Surfaces (Inspired by Tree Root Systems)\uc0\u8232 Build sidewalks with slightly flexible, shock-absorbing layered surfaces that reduce joint stress and improve balance, similar to how forest floors cushion movement and distribute pressure.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Pollination Companion Zones (Inspired by Pollinator Networks)\uc0\u8232 Encourage short-distance movement by placing attractive social and practical \'93destination flowers\'94 (mini markets, tea corners, health kiosks, social tables) at frequent intervals to make walking purposeful and rewarding.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Hibernation-Season Urban Mode (Inspired by Seasonal Adaptation)\uc0\u8232 During extreme weather seasons, automatically shift neighborhoods into \'93protected mobility mode\'94 with temporary shelters, covered paths, extra seating, and nearby mobile services\'97like ecosystems adapting for survival in winter.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Topic 2- Education\'a0
\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f0\b\fs32 Prompt1- Generate 10 innovative ideas for how education systems could evolve in the next 10 years. Focus on meaningful changes beyond current classroom models.
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf0 Answer-
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 AI-Personalized Learning Pathways\uc0\u8232 Every student gets a dynamic learning journey tailored to their pace, interests, strengths, and gaps. Instead of age-based grades, progress is based on mastery, with AI helping teachers design individualized support.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Competency-Based Graduation Instead of Seat Time\uc0\u8232 Students graduate by proving skills and understanding rather than completing a fixed number of classroom hours. Portfolios, projects, and real-world demonstrations replace many traditional exams.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 School as a Community Innovation Hub\uc0\u8232 Schools become centers where students, local businesses, nonprofits, and citizens collaborate on solving real local challenges\'97urban planning, sustainability, public health, entrepreneurship, and more.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Global Collaborative Classrooms\uc0\u8232 Students regularly work with peers from other countries through live multilingual collaboration platforms. Geography, politics, and culture are learned through direct shared projects rather than textbooks alone.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Life Skills as Core Curriculum\uc0\u8232 Financial literacy, emotional regulation, communication, negotiation, parenting basics, digital citizenship, and decision-making become required foundational subjects, not optional side lessons.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Micro-Schools + Learning Networks\uc0\u8232 Instead of one large institution, students learn through flexible networks of smaller learning environments: studios, labs, apprenticeships, online mentors, and local experts connected into one credential system.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Teacher Role Shift: From Lecturer to Learning Architect\uc0\u8232 Teachers spend less time delivering content and more time coaching, mentoring, designing experiences, and helping students develop judgment, creativity, and resilience.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Real-World Apprenticeships Starting Earlier\uc0\u8232 Teenagers spend meaningful time embedded in workplaces\'97healthcare, engineering, media, government, trades, startups\'97so career discovery starts before university decisions, not after.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Mental Health Embedded into School Design\uc0\u8232 Education systems are structured around wellbeing: flexible schedules, recovery spaces, counseling access, social-emotional coaching, and reduced performance anxiety built into assessment systems.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Lifelong Learning Accounts\uc0\u8232 Education becomes a lifelong public infrastructure. Every citizen receives a learning account they can use throughout adulthood for reskilling, certifications, career pivots, and continuous professional growth\'97not just during youth.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Prompt 2- Generate 10 ideas for transforming education that are completely unlike current systems.
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Constraints:
\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f0\b\fs32 - Do not use AI, apps, online platforms, or personalization systems
\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f0\b\fs32 - Avoid common ideas like adaptive learning, EdTech platforms, or gamification
\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f0\b\fs32 - Focus on fundamentally different ways of learning and teaching
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf0 Answer-\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f2\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cities as Schools\uc0\u8232 Replace most classroom learning with structured learning across the city itself. Markets teach economics, courts teach civics, farms teach biology, workshops teach physics, and public spaces become living textbooks.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Age-Free Learning Communities\uc0\u8232 Eliminate age-based grades entirely. Learners are grouped by responsibility, readiness, and contribution rather than birth year, creating multi-generational learning communities where younger and older students learn together.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Problem-First Education\uc0\u8232 Students never begin with subjects like math or history. They begin with real problems\'97clean water, housing, conflict, food systems\'97and subjects are learned only as tools needed to solve them.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Seasonal Learning Cycles\uc0\u8232 Education follows natural and social seasons rather than fixed semesters. Harvest seasons, elections, migration, festivals, and local industry cycles shape what is studied and when, connecting learning to lived reality.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Apprenticeship as the Default Model\uc0\u8232 Formal schooling becomes secondary. Every learner belongs primarily to a craft, profession, or public service role\'97builder, healer, organizer, artist, scientist\'97and academic knowledge emerges through participation.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Silence and Reflection Schools\uc0\u8232 Deep thinking becomes central. Large parts of education are dedicated to observation, reflection, writing, solitude, and discussion rather than constant instruction, helping students develop judgment instead of information recall.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Public Contribution Graduation\uc0\u8232 Students graduate only after completing something of lasting public value: restoring a park, writing a local history archive, designing community housing solutions, or creating a social service\'97not by passing exams.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Rotating Teacherless Houses\uc0\u8232 Small student houses run themselves with minimal formal teachers. Learners rotate responsibility for teaching, governance, conflict resolution, food systems, and collective decision-making, treating self-management as education itself.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Failure-Based Curriculum\uc0\u8232 Instead of protecting students from mistakes, schools are designed around repeated failure in meaningful work\'97building, debating, negotiating, leading, repairing\'97where reflection on failure is considered the main source of learning.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Citizenship Before Career Education\uc0\u8232 The first purpose of education becomes preparing people to govern, cooperate, and participate in society rather than preparing for jobs. Public speaking, mediation, civic duty, and collective responsibility become the foundation of schooling.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-960\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Prompt 3- Generate 10 ideas for transforming education inspired by systems from nature, biology, or unrelated fields such as logistics, gaming, or architecture.
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
