\f2\fs32 \cf0 **1. The Oral Studio Model**\'a0\'a0
\f1\fs24 \

\f2\fs32 Writing is used only for record-keeping, not instruction. All learning happens through structured oral transmission: memorization, recitation, debate, storytelling, and live demonstration. Students progress by performing knowledge aloud to a circle of elders and peers. No textbooks, no screens\'97only voice, ear, and memory.
