\f2\fs32 \cf0 **2. Apprentice Guilds Replacing Age-Based Grades**\'a0\'a0
\f1\fs24 \

\f2\fs32 Children enter mixed-age guilds at age 6 based on temperament, not age. Each guild has a master teacher who stays with the same guild for 12 years. Academic subjects are woven into craft apprenticeships (woodworking, textile arts, farming, cooking, masonry). Mastery is demonstrated by producing a physical artifact that embeds the lesson\'97e.g., a carved table that encodes geometry and local history.
