\f2\fs32 *Model:* Learning is divided into ecological phases: Phase 1 (chaotic play and exploration), Phase 2 (structured imitation and rules), Phase 3 (competitive mastery), Phase 4 (cooperative creation), Phase 5 (teaching and decomposition). A learner cannot skip phases, but they can remain in a phase indefinitely. Each phase physically alters the learning space (e.g., Phase 1 is a bare room with sand; Phase 5 includes a community garden that feeds younger phases).
