\f2\fs32 \cf0 ### 1. **Nomadic Apprenticeship Caravans**
\f1\fs24 \

\f2\fs32 Education becomes mobile tribes of 20\'9640 people (mixed ages) who travel together on foot or by simple means for months or years. Learning happens through constant movement across landscapes and cultures. Each caravan is led by master practitioners (farmers, artisans, healers, storytellers). Young people learn by living the daily realities of different trades and places\'97building shelters, tending herds, negotiating with communities\'97rather than studying subjects. Progression is marked by the distance traveled and skills visibly mastered in real survival and service contexts.
