\f2\fs32 \cf0 ### 2. **Silent Observership Years**
\f1\fs24 \

\f2\fs32 For several years (ages 12\'9616), learners enter a mandatory period of deep silence and observation. They live with elders, craftspeople, or in monasteries/convents/natural settings where speaking is minimized or forbidden for extended periods. Learning occurs through prolonged watching, listening, imitating, and absorbing without instruction or questioning. Mastery is demonstrated later through flawless replication of complex crafts or rituals learned only by observation. This rebuilds deep attention and humility as foundational capacities.
