\f1\fs24 \

\f2\fs32 Entire communities replace schools with seasonal "labor universities." Young people work full days alongside adults in essential collective tasks: farming, building infrastructure, food preservation, or caregiving. Knowledge is transmitted orally during the work itself through songs, stories, proverbs, and direct correction. There are no separate classes\'97wisdom emerges from the rhythm of labor, repetition, and shared hardship. Status comes from contribution and endurance, not knowledge accumulation.
