\f1\fs24 \

\f2\fs32 Education centers on large, multi-generational storytelling circles held daily or weekly around fires, in groves, or communal halls. Elders and master storytellers recount epics, histories, moral dilemmas, and practical knowledge embedded in narrative form. Learners do not analyze or debate initially; they internalize through repetition, memorization, and eventual retelling with their own variations. Deep understanding develops through years of hearing the same stories in different life stages, allowing layers of meaning to unfold naturally.
