\f2\fs32 \cf0 ### 1. **Mycelial Network Learning Webs** (Inspired by fungal mycelium networks)
\f1\fs24 \

\f2\fs32 Mycelium connects trees and plants underground, exchanging nutrients and signals across a decentralized web based on need. Education forms as living "mycelial webs": small, place-based groups linked through human "hyphae" (messengers or rotating facilitators) who carry knowledge, skills, and resources between clusters. No central curriculum exists; instead, communities identify local needs or surpluses (e.g., herbal knowledge in one area, crafting in another) and exchange them through reciprocal visits and shared labor. Learning spreads organically via relationship and mutual benefit, with resilience emerging from redundancy and adaptation to local conditions.
